00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:40.370
So that's why you were grilling them.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:42.460
Since we have some little kiddos with us,

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:44.460
we're going to substitute
some water for white wine.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:47.000
Oh, water works, too?

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:51.170
We'll put them into the skillet along with
some Manila clams and cherry tomatoes,

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:52.670
and apply the lid.

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:55.010
We'll let them stew
for a while and then...

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:57.300
Yes? Yes?

00:16:57.300 --> 00:17:01.770
Ta-da! We've got ourselves
some rainbow trout acqua pazza!

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:05.980
You never cease to amaze me.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:09.900
I hope that I can cook
like you some day, Koharu.

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:12.900
You've actually made our
microwave explode before, Mom.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:16.240
Oh, you're exaggerating.
It just got a little smoky.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.950
What did you two do
for your meals until now?

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:22.200
Her father was always
in charge of the meals...

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:25.250
But while he was in the hospital, we'd
have prepared dishes from the supermarket

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:27.670
or go out to eat.

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:33.720
I got even busier with work, but...
I should've worked on that.

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.470
Oh, that's totally fine!

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:36.300
But...

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:38.600
The prepared dishes from
the supermarket are great!

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:40.310
I rely on those all the time!

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:41.810
Wait, really?

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:42.720
Yes!

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:46.520
Oh, yeah. I found a place near our
house that has great side dishes.

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:48.730
Oh, really? Where?

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:51.940
No fair! It's my turn next!

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:54.150
One more time! One more!

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:57.280
Okay. One more time,
then we'll switch with Tora, okay?

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:58.160
'Kay!

00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:00.830
Promise!

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:04.870
Looks like you two found a great playmate.

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:07.370
Let's eat.

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:20.720
The fish is nice and warm.

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:23.560
Yeah, it's so fragrant and delicious!

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:32.820
Nothing beats eating a fresh one
while you're drinking a cold one.

00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:34.530
And here come the old man jokes.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:35.820
Is it yummy, Niji?

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:37.360
Yup!

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:40.910
Sorry to have you feed Niji like that...

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:42.410
--The soup is delicious.
--Oh, it's totally fine.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:42.830
--But your food's going to get cold.
--Oh, it's totally fine.

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:45.410
--But your food's going to get cold.
--There's plenty more!

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:48.500
Don't worry. Is it yummy, Niji?

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:49.960
Yup!

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:59.470
Hiyori?

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:01.640
Um... Here.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:02.800
Huh?

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:09.350
Thank you.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:15.610
Hiyori!

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:22.160
I'm gonna go get the runts to bed.

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:25.660
Okay. We should probably brush
our teeth and go to bed, too.

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.580
Yeah...

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:41.720
It immediately got cold
after leaving the campfire.

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:45.180
I put some hot-water bottles in our
sleeping bags, so just survive until then.

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.850
Oh, bless...

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:51.770
Koharu, look up at the sky.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:02.910
Wow! The sky is filled with stars!

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:07.620
Is that what they call the Big Dipper?

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:09.830
Oh, it is.

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:12.210
It looks different from my textbook.

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:13.540
Say what now?

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:16.840
Well, there's more than seven stars!

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:21.630
Oh, right. We can't see all
the smaller stars in the city.

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:27.220
I see. So they're still there
even if you can't see them.

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:32.230
Still there even if you can't see them...

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:35.190
I wonder if my dad can still recognize me.

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:39.980
Oh, I mean my actual dad.

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:44.200
After my dad died,
I suddenly grew way taller.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:48.330
So maybe he wouldn't recognize me anymore.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:50.330
Of course he will.

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:58.500
Wasn't today a lot of fun, Hiyori?

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:00.090
Yeah.

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:04.180
So don't worry.

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:09.220
I'm sure your dad and my mom

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.430
will still recognize us.

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:17.310
As long as we can
still smile like we used to.

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:33.910
Yeah.

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:50.680
Yeah.

00:21:54.350 --> 00:21:56.060
It's freezing.

00:21:56.060 --> 00:21:58.100
Koi!

00:21:59.150 --> 00:21:59.690
You need to be quiet at night
when we're camping.

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:01.860
"Shh"

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:01.860
You need to be quiet at night
when we're camping.

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:02.030
You need to be quiet at night
when we're camping.

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:03.860
Whoops, sorry.

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:06.740
Hey, let's go fishing and camping again.

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:08.990
We're already discussing next time?

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:17.370
Next time, we'll come
during autumn colors time!

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:19.290
We'll watch the leaves
fall, fish, and camp!

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:21.090
That's a mouthful.

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:22.340
True.

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:24.380
Aw...

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:32.810
<i>Even if you don't say anything</i>

00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:38.560
<i>I know how you're feeling and</i>
<i>when you're lying or telling the truth</i>

00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:41.190
<i>Even if you don't do anything</i>

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:46.190
<i>Just being next to you</i>
<i>makes the day brighter</i>

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:50.410
<i>The reason I've always loved the ocean</i>

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:55.160
<i>Is because you were always by my side</i>

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:58.370
<i>The way we laugh is becoming similar</i>

00:22:58.370 --> 00:23:03.500
<i>It's almost like we're cider</i>

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:07.720
<i>Bubble, bubble, our laughter combines</i>

00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:12.010
<i>Bubble, bubble, then floats up</i>
<i>and pops together</i>

00:23:12.010 --> 00:23:20.270
<i>We gather up the light and</i>
<i>gain even more precious things</i>

00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:24.520
<i>Bubble, bubble, our laughter combines</i>

00:23:24.520 --> 00:23:28.860
<i>Bubble, bubble, then floats up</i>
<i>and pops together</i>

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:33.830
<i>May a present where we can</i>
<i>laugh about the past and future</i>

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:41.500
<i>Always be right here</i>

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:46.500
<i>May a present where we can</i>
<i>laugh about the past and future</i>

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:52.890
<i>Always be right here</i>

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:56.350
"Next Time"

00:23:56.350 --> 00:24:00.100
"Next Time"
So, hey. Why can't you bring
bananas when you go fishing?

00:24:00.100 --> 00:24:03.560
"Next Time"
Apparently the idea comes
from when bugs would spring up

00:24:03.560 --> 00:24:06.020
"Next Time"
from bananas on boats
before there were refrigerators.

00:24:06.020 --> 00:24:07.860
"Next Time"
It's just another superstition.

00:24:07.860 --> 00:24:09.940
"Next Time"
That's bananas!
